    "yes-no": [
      {"t":"mc","q":"Which word means \"yes\" to an older person?","o":["opo","oo","po","hindi po"],"why":"opo is the polite yes; oo is for friends, siblings and children."},
      {"t":"mc","q":"Ate asks May tubig ba? (Is there water?). There is none. Best answer?","o":["Wala po.","Hindi po.","Huwag po.","Hindi pa po."],"why":"wala answers \"Is there any…?\" when there is none."},
      {"t":"mc","q":"\"Don't eat!\" (to a friend) =","o":["Huwag kang kumain!","Hindi ka kumain!","Wala kang kumain!","Hindi kumain!"],"why":"huwag means \"don't\"; hindi only means \"not\"."},
      {"t":"mc","q":"\"I'm not tired.\" =","o":["Hindi ako pagod.","Hindi pagod ko.","Huwag akong pagod.","Hindi ko pagod."],"why":"hindi means not; it goes first and ako comes right after it."},
      {"t":"mc","q":"Kumain ka na ba? (Have you eaten?) You haven't eaten yet. Answer (to a friend):","o":["Hindi pa.","Hindi na.","Huwag pa.","Oo pa."],"why":"pa means yet, so Hindi pa is \"not yet\"; Hindi na means \"not anymore\"."},
      {"t":"order","p":"I don't have any money","a":["Wala","akong","pera"],"x":["ako"],"why":"wala is linked to the pronoun with -ng: Wala akong pera."},
      {"t":"order","p":"I don't know","a":["Hindi","ko","alam"],"x":["ako"],"why":"alam takes the ng form ko, even after hindi: Hindi ko alam."},
      {"t":"order","p":"Please don't leave (polite)","a":["Huwag","po","kayong","umalis"],"x":["kayo"],"why":"The linker -ng joins kayo to the verb, and po goes right after huwag: Huwag po kayong umalis."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"May kape ba? — __ po.","p":"Is there any coffee? — There's none. (polite)","a":["Wala"],"o":["Hindi","Huwag","Opo"],"why":"wala answers \"Is there any…?\" when there is none."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"__ kang umalis.","p":"Don't leave. (to a friend)","a":["Huwag"],"o":["Hindi","Wala","Oo"],"why":"huwag is the word for \"don't\" in an instruction."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Kumain ka na ba? — Hindi __.","p":"Have you eaten? — Not yet.","a":["pa"],"o":["na","po","ba"],"why":"pa means yet: Hindi pa = not yet; Hindi na means not anymore."},
      {"t":"type","p":"We don't have any coffee (we, not you)","a":["Wala kaming kape","Kami ay walang kape"],"hint":"wala · kami · kape · kami = we, not you","x":["kami"],"why":"wala is linked to kami with -ng: Wala kaming kape."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I don't know (polite)","a":["Hindi ko po alam"],"hint":"hindi · alam · po comes after ko","x":["ako"],"why":"alam takes the ng form ko, and po comes right after ko: Hindi ko po alam."},
      {"t":"type","p":"No, not yet (polite)","a":["Hindi pa po"],"hint":"hindi · pa = yet","x":["na"],"why":"pa means yet: Hindi pa po is a polite \"not yet\"; Hindi na means not anymore."}
    ],
